    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d406-a1">

                <pb facs="0896" n="812" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg812"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 135.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Moret to Mr. Curry.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ministerio De Estado</hi></placeName>, <date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1886-10-15"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Friday.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear</hi> Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Curry</hi>:
                    The decision of the President re-establishing the 10 per cent, duties upon goods
                    and produce from the Spanish Antilles takes me by surprise.</p>
                <p>As the point was being discussed between ourselves, it is not easy to explain the
                    act of the President without any hint or intimation from you.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>After it I think nothing is to be done, but I will refrain to take any step
                    without knowing your own mind.</p>
                <p>For that reason, and despite my bad health, you will oblige me by calling at 5
                    o’clock at the foreign office, if such time is convenient for you.</p>
                <p>Yours, sincerely,</p>
                <closer><signed>S. MORET.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
